# Claim the Kingdom's landfall ability targets a creature you control, and the plan counter is part of the same ability
# (CR 603.3d, 608.2b). Bot1's Forest enters on turn 1 with no creature on its side: the ability has no target and is
# removed from the stack, so no plan counter. On turn 3 its Fabled Passage enters with the Ornithopter as the target, and
# Bot2 Lightning Bolts the Ornithopter in response: the ability's only target is gone, so it does nothing - no plan counter
# either. The Plains the Passage then finds enters with no creature to target again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Claim the Kingdom
Forest
Fabled Passage
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Plains
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Claim the Kingdom.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Claim the Kingdom.Counters.Plan = (absent)
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Fabled Passage.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Claim the Kingdom.Counters.Plan = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Fabled Passage.Activate
Bot1.Search(Plains)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Claim the Kingdom.Counters.Plan = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Fabled Passage; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Claim the Kingdom; Forest; Plains
